INSERT INTO blog_post_translations
  (post_id, locale, slug, title, excerpt, body_html, seo_title, seo_description)
VALUES (
  :post_id, 'en', $x$genshin-impact-banners-guide$x$,
  $x$Genshin Impact banners: which one to wish on$x$,
  $x$Which banner to wish on for a character, how pity and the 50/50 work, and how many Primogems to save so none of them are wasted.$x$,
$x$<h2>Key points</h2>
<ul>
<li>Want a specific character? Wish only on their event banner. The weapon and standard banners have different rewards and their own counters.</li>
<li>A 5★ is guaranteed by wish 90, a 4★ at least once every 10 wishes.</li>
<li>Because of the 50/50, the character you want can take up to 180 wishes.</li>
<li>A wish costs 160 Primogems: up to 14,400 for one 5★ guarantee and up to 28,800 for the character you want. Genesis Crystals convert into Primogems 1:1.</li>
</ul>
<p>Wishes in Genshin Impact are more predictable than they look. Once you know how pity and the 50/50 are counted, you can budget in advance and wish for a goal instead of on luck.</p>
<h2>Banner types</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Character event banner.</strong> Higher odds for the current version's 5★ and 4★ characters. Usually two run at once and share one pity counter.</li>
<li><strong>Weapon event banner.</strong> Higher odds for two 5★ weapons. Its own counter; a 5★ is guaranteed by wish 80. You pick the weapon you want with Epitomized Path. Worth it only for a specific build.</li>
<li><strong>Standard banner.</strong> Permanent, with the base pool of 5★ characters and weapons. Its counter is separate from the event ones.</li>
</ul>
<p>Hunting a character? Wish on their event banner. The weapon and standard banners have other rewards and their own counters.</p>
<h2>Pity and the 50/50</h2>
<p>Pity is the counter that stops you from wishing forever with nothing to show for it:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>5★ by wish 90 at the latest.</strong> The base rate is about 0.6% a wish, but from roughly wish 74 it climbs steeply (&quot;soft pity&quot;), so most 5★ land between wish 74 and 90.</li>
<li><strong>4★ at least once every 10 wishes.</strong> A separate counter.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>The 50/50.</strong> When a 5★ drops on a character banner, it is either the featured character or a random standard one, roughly evenly. Lose it, and your next 5★ is guaranteed to be the featured character. You cannot lose the 50/50 twice in a row.</p>
<p>Since version 5.0 the game has Capturing Radiance: after several lost 50/50s in a row, your odds of winning the next one go up.</p>
<p><strong>Pity carries over.</strong> Progress on the character banner survives a banner change: 50 wishes without a 5★ on the last banner means you start the next one at 50.</p>
<h2>New characters or reruns: who to save for</h2>
<p>Banners change about every three weeks: each version has two phases. The current phase's schedule is in the game's own Wish screen.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>A new character's debut</strong> is the most valuable banner if you play hard content: new characters often set the meta.</li>
<li><strong>A rerun</strong> is worth catching if the character has been away a while and your team needs them: many come back only once every few versions.</li>
<li><strong>Skip</strong> a banner whose character duplicates a role you already have. Primogems saved on one banner often decide whether you can afford the next.</li>
</ul>
<p>Play Honkai: Star Rail too? The logic is the same; see <a href="/en/blog/honkai-star-rail-top-up">Honkai: Star Rail: how to top up and what to buy</a>.</p>
<h2>How many Primogems you need</h2>
<p>One wish is one fate, and one fate is 160 Primogems.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>10 wishes:</strong> 1,600 Primogems — at least one 4★.</li>
<li><strong>One 5★ guarantee (90 wishes):</strong> up to 14,400 Primogems. Soft pity usually makes it less.</li>
<li><strong>The character for certain (up to 180 wishes):</strong> up to 28,800 Primogems — if you lose the 50/50.</li>
</ul>
<p>Count from the goal and subtract what you have: your current pity and Primogems from quests and events. Only buy the difference, and keep a small reserve in case the 50/50 goes against you.</p>
<p>Genesis Crystal packages and which is better value: <a href="/en/blog/genshin-impact-genesis-crystals">Genesis Crystals in Genshin Impact</a>. Choosing between a small and a large package: <a href="/en/blog/which-top-up-package-is-better">a separate guide</a>.</p>
<h2>How to top up in soʻm on YuPay</h2>
<p>The <a href="/en/store/genshin-impact">Genshin Impact page</a> has Genesis Crystals from 60 to 8,080 and the Blessing of the Welkin Moon.</p>
<ol>
<li>Enter your UID and server — no password needed.</li>
<li>Choose a package.</li>
<li>Pay in soʻm with Click, Payme or Uzum. The total in soʻm is shown before you pay.</li>
</ol>
<p>The crystals reach your account automatically. Convert them into Primogems in the in-game shop and wish on the banner you chose.</p>$x$,
  $x$Genshin Impact banners: pity, 50/50 and how much to save$x$,
  $x$Which Genshin Impact banner to wish on: how pity and the 50/50 work, how many Primogems a character takes, and how to buy Genesis Crystals in soʻm.$x$
);

